(5246288, 762020, 30861, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sempermarine:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m actually disappointed with the score. Oh well.<br/> <br/>If you gave me a 3,2, or 1 I''d be very interested in knowing why and how I can improve in your eyes. Thanks </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I didn''t vote this challenge, but to answer your question: Image is seriously oversharpened (see the halo around the bulb?): it looks like this may have been the best of your many attempts but it wasn''t as sharp as you''d have liked it, so you gave it a heavy dosing of USM. <br/> <br/>Another thing would be backlash against liquid-drop shots, which I believe we''re starting to see. To score really well, it seems to me, they need a sense of luminosity which this one, unfortunately, is lacking.<br/> <br/>Finally, this may just be me, but the border here is doing you no favors at all, it''s sort of clumsy/chunky. If the inline were only 1 pixel, that would help a lot.</td>', 'Originally posted by sempermarine: I''m actually disappointed with the score. Oh well. If you gave me a 3,2, or 1 I''d be very interested in knowing why and how I can improve in your eyes. Thanks   I didn''t vote this challenge, but to answer your question: Image is seriously oversharpened (see the halo around the bulb?): it looks like this may have been the best of your many attempts but it wasn''t as sharp as you''d have liked it, so you gave it a heavy dosing of USM.  Another thing would be backlash against liquid-drop shots, which I believe we''re starting to see. To score really well, it seems to me, they need a sense of luminosity which this one, unfortunately, is lacking. Finally, this may just be me, but the border here is doing you no favors at all, it''s sort of clumsy/chunky. If the inline were only 1 pixel, that would help a lot.', '2009-02-09 03:24:22.000000', NULL, 0),
